- The preview (`preview_controller.js`) runs in the browser on the active
  questions, embedded as JSON. Nothing is posted or stored. Only the current
  step is in the DOM, so "Correct!", "Next question" and similar texts appear once.

## Contract with the QA auto-tests

The tests find elements by the labels in the task: visible text, `<label>`,
placeholder or `aria-label`. Keep these exactly:

- Quizzes: "New quiz" (a real `<button>`, a GET form), "Title", "Save quiz",
  "Settings" (link), "Preview" (link), "Add question" (`<button>`, GET form),
  "Delete quiz" (button + native confirm).
- Question form: "Question"; option rows with text fields "Option N"
  (`aria-label` and placeholder) and checkboxes "Option N is correct"
  (`aria-label`, plus a visually hidden label text; the visible text is
  "Correct"); "Add option"; "Active"; "Save question". Rows are renumbered when
  one is removed ("Remove option N").
- Question card (`<li>`): "Move up" / "Move down" (icon buttons with
  `aria-label`, disabled at the ends), "Active" (checkbox, saves on change),
  "Edit" (link), "Delete" (button + native confirm).
- Preview: "Question 1 of 3", option buttons (accessible name = option text;
  the letter is `aria-hidden`), "Correct!" / "Wrong!", "Next question",
  "See score", "Score: 2/3", "Start over".
- Lists: only quizzes and questions are `<li>`. Option chips are spans, so
  counting list items counts questions.
- Strings that would collide with labels are avoided elsewhere (e.g. buttons
  whose names contain a "+" or "←" keep that part `aria-hidden`).

## Verifying

- `bin/rails test:all` runs model, integration and system tests. System tests
  drive headless Chromium through Cuprite (`CHROMIUM_PATH`, default
  `/usr/bin/chromium`) and use the same labels as the QA suite.
- Design check: the mockup PNGs are renders of the mockup HTML at 1440 px wide.
  Screenshot a page at 1440 px with Ferrum and diff it against the PNG in
  horizontal bands (e.g. with the `chunky_png` gem, outside the Gemfile). The
  quiz page and the question form match except for antialiasing and the
  "Option N" placeholders, which double as test labels.
- Label check: Chromium's accessibility tree (CDP `Accessibility.queryAXTree`
  with `accessibleName` and `role`) finds every control by its exact name, the
  way Playwright's `getByRole(..., { exact: true })` does.
/*
 * Quizzy app styles. quizzy.css is the design's stylesheet (copied from
 * docs/mockups as is); this file adapts it to the markup the app renders.
 */

/* Rails' button_to wraps each button in a form: keep them inline. */
form.button_to { display: inline-flex; margin: 0; }
.buttons form.button_to { display: contents; }

.btn[disabled] { pointer-events: auto; cursor: not-allowed; }
.btn[disabled]:hover { background: inherit; color: inherit; }
.btn--ghost[disabled]:hover { background: transparent; color: var(--c-blue); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--c-blue); }


.page-head h1 { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }

/* ---------- Quiz list ---------- */

/* The whole card is clickable; the link itself is the title, so its name is the quiz title. */
.quiz-tile { position: relative; margin-bottom: 0; }
.quiz-tile h3 { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.quiz-tile__link { text-decoration: none; }
.quiz-tile__link::after { content: ""; position: absolute; inset: 0; border-radius: inherit; }
.quiz-tile:hover { color: var(--c-blue); }
.quiz-tile:hover .quiz-tile__link { color: var(--c-pink); }
.quiz-tile:has(.quiz-tile__link:focus-visible) { outline: 3px solid var(--c-pink); outline-offset: 2px; }
.quiz-tile__link:focus-visible { outline: none; }

/* ---------- Question card ---------- */

.question-list > li { list-style: none; }
.question-item__content { min-width: 0; }
.question-item__body { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.question-item__num { cursor: default; }

/* The mockup's option chips, as spans (only quizzes and questions are list items). */
.question-item__options { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; }
.question-item__option {
  display: inline-block;
  background: var(--c-lavender);
  border-radius: 1000px;
  padding: 4px 12px;
  font-size: 15px;
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}
.question-item__option.is-correct { background: var(--c-success); color: var(--c-white); }


.question-item__activation { margin: 0; display: flex; }

@media (max-width: 720px) {
  .question-item { grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; }
  .question-item__actions { grid-column: 1 / -1; flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; }
}

/* ---------- Question form ---------- */

.option-row__correct { white-space: nowrap; }
/* A switch inside a .field keeps the switch style, not the field-label style. */
.field label.checkbox { font-weight: 500; font-size: inherit; }
.option-rows__add { margin-bottom: 28px; }
.option-rows:empty { display: none; }

/* ---------- Settings ---------- */

.danger-zone { margin-top: 48px; }
.danger-zone h3 { margin-bottom: 0.3em; }

/* ---------- Preview (player view on a phone) ---------- */

/* The banner and the phone column fill the screen together. */
.preview-page { display: flex; flex-direction: column; min-height: 100vh; min-height: 100dvh; }
.preview-page > .play { flex: 1; width: 100%; min-height: 0; }

.play__quiz-title { text-align: right; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.play-option:disabled { cursor: default; }
button.play-option:disabled:hover { box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px transparent; }
.play-feedback:empty { display: none; }
.play-actions { margin-top: 20px; display: flex; }
.play-next { flex: 1; }
.play__footer { display: flex; justify-content: center; margin-top: 24px; }
.play .result-card__place { margin-bottom: 12px; }

/* ---------- Home ---------- */


.home__text p { margin-bottom: 1.2em; }
